course: dictionary
lesson: 12327
title: Pushing back with counteract
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To counteract something means to act against it so that it has less effect, or no effect at all. «Exercise helps counteract sitting all day.» Sitting still for hours can cause problems, and exercise pushes back against those problems.
explain: Look for the clue in the sentence. «The doctor gave her medicine to counteract the poison.» The medicine is working against the poison, so the poison has less effect. The poison is the thing being worked against.
explain: The word counter means against, so counteract means to act against. Other words built the same way are counterattack and counterweight. When you meet counteract, ask yourself: what is working against what?
fact: Counteract is a verb: counteract, counteracts, counteracted, counteracting.
fact: To counteract something means to act against it so that it has less effect or no effect.
fact: The phrase «counteract the effects of» is useful: «Sunscreen helps counteract the effects of the hot sun.»
fact: In science, an alkali can counteract an acid, which means it neutralises it.
fact: People can counteract bad habits with good ones, such as going for a walk to counteract too much screen time.
exercise: «Exercise helps counteract sitting all day.» What does counteract mean here? | Forgets about sitting | Makes sitting last longer | *Works against sitting, so it does less harm | Joins together with sitting
exercise: «The doctor gave her medicine to counteract the poison.» What is the medicine doing to the poison? | *Acting against it so it has less effect | Making it stronger | Pouring it away | Ignoring it completely
exercise: Sam wears a coat to counteract the cold wind. Why does he wear it? | To hide from his friends | To make the wind colder | *To reduce the effect of the cold on him | To dry his hair
test: Which phrase best means counteract? | *Act against | Copy | Speed up | Add to
test: Ella eats fruit to counteract the tiredness after school. What is she trying to do? | Forget her lunch | *Reduce the tiredness | Make herself more tired | Fall asleep faster
exam: Pick the sentence where counteract is used correctly: | *Mia drinks water to counteract the effects of the hot day | The dog counteracted of the park | Counteract is a blue bicycle | Mia sang counteract the song
